  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 PM CDT Wed Jun 3 2026\n\nWednesday night through Tuesday:\n\nAn Omega-block will establish over the the Great Lakes and \nprogress south over the week, resulting in widespread ridging over\nthe southeast CONUS. An isolated shower will be possible in the \nsouthwest this afternoon as the the ridge sets up over the area. \nAs the blocking pattern/ridge gets established over our region, \nearly summer temps with dry air, conditions won't be as \noppressive. The block will gradually break and move the ridge \neastward and an upper- lvl trough off to the west will increasing \nmoisture over the region Friday into the weekend. Embedded \ndisturbances will increase shower/storm chances late Friday in the\nsouth. Widespread rain chances will begin Saturday and continue \ninto the new week each as deeper moisture filters in beyond the \nextended period. /SW/",
